- op: discuss  # 76f0
  at: '2026-09-02T07:37:57Z'  # 76f0
  by: agent  # 76f0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 76f0
  clock: 4  # 76f0
  nonce: 76f0  # 76f0
  message: "PRIORITY P2 -> P3 on owner authorisation, 2026-09-02. Recording the reasoning\nhere because a re-rank that lives only in conversation is indistinguishable\nnext session from drift.\n\nTWO MEASURED FACTS ARGUE FOR IT, both from this item's own discharged\nprecondition:\n\n  * INERTNESS. The deliverable this item guessed at -- the missing far-end rows\n    -- cannot fire. Every category-B far-end call lands on the `external`\n    sentinel in the module slot, and the candidate rows match perfectly at\n    every RESOLVED slot, so adding them changes nothing until receiver typing\n    lands. A row added today would create the appearance of coverage with none.\n  * POPULATION. ~40 sites over 18 repositories, bounded from ABOVE (receivers\n    not verified to come from a launch): python 11, go 5, c 0, java ~24 of 141\n    getInputStream sites once the java.net.Socket receivers are excluded.\n\nNeither fact was known when this was ranked P2 -- the item was filed with the\nrows as its expected deliverable and no emission measurement behind it.\n\nWHAT WOULD RAISE IT AGAIN, stated so the deferral has a written re-open\ntrigger: receiver typing from a local binding landing for python/java/go (the\nmechanism WI-lipis shipped for go's bufio.NewScanner argument origin). The\nmoment that lands, these rows stop being inert and this item becomes a small\ncatalogue change with a measured population behind it."  # 76f0
